# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local configuration — the real artifact paths live here, NEVER committed.
.env
.env.*
.envrc
*.local
*.local.*
config.local.*
local/

# Anything that authenticates you to your node. The manual tells you to copy
# the cookie file across when the node is on another machine, and a copy made
# inside a clone is a copy git would otherwise offer to commit.
.cookie
*.cookie
*.pem
*.key
*.asc
*.gpg
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# Assistant and editor configuration. The first is doctrine: the reference is
# readable code, spec and tests, so no tool's harness belongs in here — and
# without this rule only the files whose NAME happens to match `*.local.*`
# would be caught, which is luck, not a rule. The rest carry absolute paths
# from the machine they were written on, which is the same leak by another
# route.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Heavy data and artifacts — nodsig holds ONLY code plus small, public
# fixtures. Graph, index and derivatives (hundreds of GB) live OUTSIDE the
# repository, referenced through local configuration that is not committed.
data/
artifacts/
runs/
locks_*/
# (the test fixtures, small and public, stay tracked under tests/fixtures/)

# The address check's output, which lists the addresses SOMEONE ASKED ABOUT
# and is written next to wherever the command was run — including inside a
# clone. The tool says it is sensitive; git should not then offer to commit
# it into a public repository.
#
# Both names stay. The default was `verdicts.txt` once, and a clone that
# still holds one, or a shell history that still writes one, must not stop
# being covered because the default moved.
check-results.txt
verdicts.txt

# `check --csv <path>` writes the same answers under a name YOU choose, so no
# fixed name can cover it: the whole extension goes instead. Nothing in this
# repository is a tracked CSV, and the ones the tools write (the reuse curve,
# the per-block series, the census) are outputs, not sources. A public fixture
# would need the exception below rather than a silent commit.
*.csv
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv

# A run's log carries the artifact paths it was given and the node URL it
# talked to, which is the machine's own topology written down line by line.
*.log

# Local agent instructions: private, never published.
CLAUDE.md
